{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06674 - MONDO_grouped_5306_20655",
  "verbalization": "Golimumab is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ankylosing Spondylitis (AS) through a multi-step pathway involving the treatment of spondyloarthropathy, a condition that predisposes individuals to AS. The evidence suggests that Golimumab, through its indication for spondyloarthropathy, may influence the immune system in a manner that reduces inflammation and mitigates the progression of AS. This is supported by the indirect link between Golimumab and AS via Etanercept and Certolizumab Pegol, both of which are known to target inflammatory pathways and are used in the management of AS. The overlapping indications and the shared role in modulating immune responses highlight a potential mechanism by which Golimumab could contribute to the treatment of AS. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of targeting inflammatory processes in spondyloarthropathy to address the underlying pathophysiology of AS.",
